// mlx-cc's code generation epoch: what `mlx build` keys the objects
// mlx-cc made by, instead of mlx-cc's own bytes (`mlx-cc --codegen-epoch`
// prints it; `--codegen-epoch=FILE` writes the stamp build.mlx's
// `mlx-cc-epoch` step makes, which every object step names with
// Build.programEpoch). So a change to mlx-cc that does not change the
// object of any unit that already compiled keeps every object in the
// result cache valid, and a rebuild after it compiles only the steps
// that failed before (and those whose sources changed).
//
// THE RULE: bump CODEGEN_EPOCH in the same commit as any change that can
// change the bytes of an object (or a dependency file) for a source that
// compiled before the change:
//
//   - code generation, instruction selection, register or stack layout;
//   - the ABI: calling convention, struct and class layout, vtables,
//     thunks, RTTI, exceptions, thread-locals, bit-fields;
//   - name mangling, the symbols an object defines or needs, their
//     binding (weak/local), what an object holds (inline functions,
//     vtables, instances made or left out), their order;
//   - constant evaluation (constexpr results, sizeof/alignof, enum
//     values, initializers computed at compile time), overload or
//     template choices that pick another function;
//   - the predefined macros, the headers mlx-cc ships that are read as
//     part of the unit (they are inputs too, by the depfile, but a
//     header's meaning moved into the compiler is not), the object
//     format (relocatable.mlx), the `@at` line-table symbols, the -MD
//     dependency file's contents.
//
// No bump for a change that only
//
//   - makes code compile that failed to before (a missing feature, a
//     bug that stopped the compile): those units had no object;
//   - makes compiling faster or leaner with the same output (the
//     lookups, memos and arenas of docs/internals/build-time-notes.md);
//   - changes diagnostics, warnings, the crash report's wiring, the
//     driver's options, -E's output, the linker (mlx-ld is a program of
//     its own, keyed by its bytes) or MLX_CC_STATS.
//
// When in doubt, bump: a bump costs one full rebuild, a missing one
// leaves stale objects in every cache. `mlx build --verify-epoch N`
// compiles N objects the cache holds again with the current mlx-cc and
// fails when one differs (tools/check_codegen_epoch.sh runs it).
// 2: the unit read in two parts (the -include files parsed before the
//    file is preprocessed), the prefix's lambdas and unnamed namespace
//    named after the prefix's options, the arena's layout (the command
//    line's memory apart, -MD's text made at once): objects differ in
//    lambda names and in the compiler addresses left in relocated words.
// 3: the M3 line's code generation joined (webkit-m3): static_cast to a
//    class constructs it, a branch's temporaries live to the end of the
//    full expression (flags), elided braced temporaries, a converted
//    conditional branch made at the result, explicit no-op destructor
//    calls, anonymous struct members in a constructor's list, 128-bit
//    values not constant, the deduced result buffer.
// 4: a constexpr call's pointer into a global in a global's initializer
//    (`values.data()` of a std::array) is a relocation, not the
//    evaluator's tagged address.
// 5: an unscoped enum argument promotes to int in overload ranking; a
//    braced assignment `x = { a, b }` constructs through a constructor
//    template that takes the values as they are.
// 6: a class template's instance named through a reference while an
//    argument is declared only is not made then (it had no size, and a
//    function returning it took no result buffer).
// 7: a function template's instance for a pointer to a function deduced
//    from the pointer's parameter types as they are (a generic lambda's
//    `auto` parameter for a reference one).
// 8: a class returned by a `decltype(auto)` (or `const auto`) function
//    made in the caller's buffer; `c ? f() : g()` of a class has each
//    call write its result at the expression's (neither moved by its
//    bytes); `V v { n }` takes V's size constructor when no element of
//    its initializer_list is made from the number n.
// 9: ++ and -- of a class with no operator++ through its conversion to
//    a reference (a range-for's step too); mlxlibcpp's ranges projections
//    keep a returned reference.
// 10: a condition declaring a reference tests the object it refers to.
// 11: a scoped enum converts implicitly to no type in overload ranking
//    (a constrained template for enums over `operator<<(uint8_t)`:
//    WTF::Persistence::Encoder's, scopedenumoverload).
// 12: a bit-field of an enum whose underlying type is bool reads back
//    zero-extended (ScriptElement's ParserInserted, boolenumbitfield).
// 13: a data member hides a base's member function of its name when
//    named unqualified in a member function (ConcurrentPtrHashSet's
//    Table read TrailingArray's `size` function's address as its size:
//    the collector's opaque root table filled up, datamemberhides).
// 14: inline assembly calls a symbol (libpas's double-free check in
//    pas_segregated_page_inlines.h, as released: a relocation, the stack
//    16-byte aligned at the call) and stores and loads the MXCSR;
//    <mmintrin.h>, <xmmintrin.h> and <emmintrin.h> complete, their types
//    unions of lanes, 16-byte aligned (SIMDe's native SSE2 path, which
//    WebKit's SIMDHelpers.h takes on x86-64): inlineasm, ssebaseline.
// 15: argument-dependent lookup of a nested class's operand looks in the
//    namespace around the classes around it, not in the class around it:
//    an `operator==` (or a function of the name) that is a member of the
//    class around was taken and the nested class's hidden friend not
//    seen (WebCore's ScrollingStateNode.h: LayerRepresentation's
//    defaulted == of its GraphicsLayerData, nestedfriendadl); calls that
//    bound the member before bind the namespace's function now.
// 16: an object of a class with a vtable made by the implicit copy
//    constructor gets its own class's vtable pointers after its bases and
//    members (a base's copy constructor stored the base's; a sliced
//    source's bytes held its derived class's): WebCore's animation values'
//    clone() (implicitcopyvptr).
// 17: decltype of a qualified member whose qualifier has template
//    arguments (`decltype(std::remove_pointer<E>::type::value)`) is the
//    member's declared type, not a reference (ANGLE's PackParam,
//    decltypequalifiedmember); a data member assigned or accessed
//    unqualified in a member function hides a type of its name around
//    the class (`Type = ...` of ANGLE's VertexAttribCurrentValueData
//    beside gl::Type, datamemberhidestype).
// 18: a constructor's list naming members of an anonymous struct inside
//    an anonymous union makes each at its own offset (both were made at
//    the struct's: ANGLE's DeviceQueueIndex, anonstructinunion); `U u =
//    {}` of a union whose first member is an aggregate is zero
//    (unionemptybraces); an explicit specialization of a class template's
//    plain conversion function for one instance (specializedconversion).
// 19: a file's unnamed namespace is named after its path even when its
//    -include prefix opened one (named after the prefix): the files of
//    one prefix had their unnamed namespaces' classes and functions under
//    one name (ANGLE's prefix, libANGLE/Debug.h; its translator's
//    Traverser classes, defined many times; check_cpp.sh's two files).
// 20: a member of a partial specialization defined after instances of
//    it were made (an explicit instantiation's among them) is made for
//    them too, as a primary template's is: ANGLE's
//    SetFloatUniformMatrixGLSL<2, 4>::Run was left undefined
//    (partialmemberlate).
// 21: `f<args>` of several function templates of the name, not called,
//    is the set of their instances, a pointer to a function's type
//    choosing (it was the first template's: ANGLE's
//    Initialize4ComponentData, overloadedtemplateaddress); an alias chosen
//    for such a pointer is its function.
// 22: a union is copied as its bytes by its implicit copy constructor
//    and assignment (they went member by member when a member's class
//    had constructors, leaving bytes behind: bison's YYSTYPE of ANGLE's
//    GLSL parser, unioncopybytes).
// 23: a copy constructor of a class template's instance defaulted
//    outside the class copies the members (ANGLE's FixedVector copied
//    as an empty one): outofclassdefault.
// 24: a free operator binding an rvalue object as it is beats a base's
//    member operator equal on the operand, and `a << b` of a temporary
//    or an rvalue reference keeps it an rvalue (WebCore's
//    `(std::ostringstream() << x).str()`): rvaluestream.
// 25: `f<args>` of several templates takes those the arguments cover
//    (std::min<double>: explicittemplatedefaults); a conversion operator
//    to a reference makes its class (a template's instance) to bind a
//    base (refconversionbase); a constructor template's own pack weighed
//    for class template argument deduction does not fit, an error no
//    more (ctadconstructorpack).
// 26: a braced list of one element given for an initializer_list
//    parameter fits the list whose element it converts to, not another's
//    (ANGLE's SeparateDeclarations: `float c = a, s = b;` crashed its
//    translator): initlistoverload.
// 27: mlxlibcpp's std::remove_if and std::unique move the elements they
//    keep (they copied them: unique_ptrs copied by their bytes, the
//    erased tail then freeing the kept ones, Skia's SkSL module loader
//    reading freed elements, Ganesh's first shader), and an assignment
//    that takes a deleted copy or move assignment is an error, no longer
//    the implicit assignment's bytes: removeifuniqueptr,
//    deletedassignment.
// 28: `new (arg) T` with one argument that is no address calls the
//    operator new taking it (the argument was taken for the address:
//    Skia's `new (uniformSize) GrSkSLFP(...)`, its
//    GrProcessor::operator new(size_t, size_t), built at address 0):
//    placementnewsize.
// 29: a non-const lvalue reference parameter does not take an argument
//    of another type (not a class: its conversion operator is weighed as
//    before), which would be converted into a temporary: `fFlags &=
//    flags` of a uint32_t is the built-in &=, not Skia's
//    `operator&=(Flags &, Flags)` on a temporary (GrFragmentProcessor's
//    flags never cleared, Ganesh calling an override no class had):
//    lvaluereferencetype.
// 30: a class template's instance named as a member function's result
//    is made when needed whole, not with the class read (made while
//    that class was being made, it laid the class out as nothing:
//    skvx::Vec<2,float>'s `Vec<4,T> xyxy()` made Vec<4,float> with both
//    its Vec<2,float> halves at offset 0, offsetof(float4, hi) 0,
//    Ganesh's anti-aliased paths drawing nothing): memberresultinstance.
//    And an instance named before it is made, then made in place, is
//    listed once among its template's instances: a member template's
//    definition read after it was applied to it twice, the second time
//    to another constructor template of as many parameters (JSC's
//    AuxiliaryBarrier<Butterfly *> left with no constructor taking
//    WriteBarrierEarlyInit): memberdefinitionlater.
//    (Also retires the objects of epochs 27-29 that compilers between
//    those commits left in the shared cache.)
// 31: an overloaded function's name for a reference to a function (a
//    parameter, a variable, a member, a static_cast) is the overload of
//    the reference's signature, not the first declared (WTF's
//    interleave(list, serialize, ", "_s) called MQ::serialize of a
//    MediaQueryList for each MediaQuery: MediaQueryList::media() empty,
//    Voyager crashing when the desktop's scheme changed):
//    functionreferenceoverload.
// 32: the assembler (asm.mlx) relaxes jumps to labels of the text to
//    rel8 as GNU as does (inline assembly's bytes change), and assembles
//    top-level asm statements into the object (they were skipped:
//    LowLevelInterpreter.cpp's interpreter, MacroAssemblerX86_64.cpp's
//    probe trampolines): fileasm. An enumerator named through aliases of
//    a namespace's typedef-named unnamed enum (`GPRReg::InvalidGPRReg`):
//    typedefenumalias. The assembler's instructions without operands
//    from movsd (the string move, missing from its list) on had the
//    next one's bytes: pushfq was std, lodsb movsq (fileasm).
// 33: JavaScriptCore's Baseline JIT and DFG compiled (ENABLE_JIT,
//    ENABLE_DFG_JIT): a class's `using Base::f;` joins the base's own
//    using-declared functions too (usingbaseusing), and a qualified name
//    in a derived class finds a class's own overloads before its
//    using-declaration's (qualifiedusingown); an alias template's
//    defaults name its namespace's templates (aliasdefaultnamespace); a
//    generic lambda in a lambda captures `this` through the outer one
//    (genericlambdainlambdathis); a template's move constructor and
//    assignment move an rvalue of a class deleting its copies
//    (templatemovedeletedcopy); unary -, ~ and + of a class convert it
//    (unaryclassconversion); a base instance's template parameters are
//    not inherited (baseparameternotinherited); make_index_sequence
//    nests log N deep and calls and lists take 4096 arguments
//    (longindexsequence); ranges::lower_bound defaults its comparison
//    (rangeslowerboundprojection); partial ordering weighs the
//    parameters given arguments (partialorderinggiven); CTAD from an
//    object of the template's own takes its class (ctadowninstance); a
//    function deduces a `T *` (functionpointerpattern); an empty fold's
//    parenthesized pattern is skipped (emptyfoldparenthesized); a
//    member template's explicit call weighs the base templates its
//    class's using-declaration names (usingbasetemplateexplicit); a
//    default argument's names are looked up where it was written
//    (defaultargumentlexicalscope); auto value packs, braced copies of
//    aggregates, explicit defaulted template arguments, inherited enum
//    qualifiers, compound assignment of a class operand, members before
//    bases and folds in nested instances (autopackvalues,
//    bracedaggregatecopy, explicitdefaultedinstance,
//    inheritedenumqualifier, compoundclassoperand, memberbeforebase,
//    nestedfoldinstance).
// 34: an object of a class without a copy constructor of its own is
//    copied member by member, not by a constructor taking another type
//    through a conversion (JSC's HandlerInfo moved by Vector called
//    CodeLocationLabel(void *) through CodePtr's deleted conversion
//    template, left undefined): copynotconverting.
// 35: a member template's instance named without a call before the
//    template's definition (its address given) is made once that is
//    read (JSC's JIT thunks were left undefined): lateaddressinstance.
// 36: an object of a derived class made into its base is copied as
//    its base part, not given to a constructor taking a scalar through a
//    conversion template, and a condition takes a class's conversion to
//    bool before a conversion template's instance (none non-const on a
//    const object): JSC's CodePtr<tag>(label) called CodePtr's deleted
//    `template <class T> operator T()`: derivedtobasecopy.
// 37: a class whose members take no bytes (std::array<T, 0>) is returned
//    and passed in an integer register, as an empty class is (it was an
//    SSE class, returned in xmm0 and stored as 8 bytes into its one, over
//    the caller's saved rbp): emptyarrayreturn.
// 38: static member functions compared by their parameters (the first
//    was passed over as `this`): a using-declaration's
//    `invert(RelationalCondition)` was hidden by a class's own static
//    `invert(DoubleCondition)` (JSC's MacroAssembler, the DFG's
//    branches): usingstaticoverload.
// 39: `C(C &&) = default` and `C &operator=(C &&) = default` beside a
//    declared copy constructor or assignment move an rvalue member by
//    member (it was copied: the DFG's switch tables, moved FixedVectors
//    its code points into, were copies): defaultedmovebesidecopy.
// 40: the built-in operator is a candidate beside the operator functions
//    ([over.match.oper]): a class converting to unsigned minus an
//    unsigned is the built-in subtraction, not LayoutUnit's `operator-(
//    int, const LayoutUnit &)` through two conversions (WebCore's cssjit
//    StackAllocator: the selector JIT's stack offsets in sixty-fourths,
//    a slot read a byte off): builtinoperatorcandidate. A file-scope
//    using-directive applies in its namespace only, a block's reaches a
//    lambda in a lambda (usingdirectivescope); a non-template base's
//    member type hides a namespace's name in a class template's instance
//    (basetypedefininstance); `new T[n] {a, b}` and placed arrays
//    (arraynewbraced); defaulted comparisons are constexpr
//    (defaultedcomparisonconstexpr); `C x(LT<float>::f())` makes an
//    object (templateidcallnotdeclarator); an empty pack's expansion in
//    braces is no element (emptypackarrayinit); `x.~W<T, U>()`
//    (explicitdestructortemplateid); designated members of an anonymous
//    union (designatedanonymousunion); mlxlibcpp's scoped_lock of several
//    mutexes, std::lock, std::try_lock (scopedlockmany); attributes after
//    `extern "C"` (externcattribute). (JavaScriptCore's B3, Air, FTL and
//    WebAssembly met the last ones.)
// 41: conversion functions are chosen as [over.match.best] has it: one
//    that is no template before a template's instance, a template
//    converting to `R<To>` before one converting to a bare `To` (JSC's
//    ExceptionOperationImplicitResult made every JIT operation's
//    ExceptionOperationResult by the bare one, of its value alone, the
//    exception lost: a direct eval's exception escaped its try):
//    conversiontemplateordering. `c ? T(a) : T(b)` makes each branch's
//    temporary at the result by its constructor, not moved there by its
//    bytes (the DFG's CallLinkStatus pointed into a dead temporary's
//    inline buffer, freed as heap): conditionalinlinebuffer.
// 42: the inline assembler knows the VEX.128 forms of the packed SSE
//    instructions (vpaddb ... vblendvps, vcmpPREDps, the shifts by an
//    immediate; asm.mlx's vexPacked) and SSE4.1's pmovsx and pmovzx:
//    WebAssembly's SIMD in JavaScriptCore's in-place interpreter (with
//    the FTL and WebAssembly on). Every form of LLIntAssembly.h's is
//    encoded as GNU as encodes it: asmavx. A constrained parameter's
//    unqualified concept is read by its namespace's qualified name
//    (FTLLowerDFGToB3.cpp's `isFunction Func1` beside a later member
//    function isFunction): conceptshadowedbymember. Directives among a
//    function-like macro's arguments are done as they are read
//    (WasmBBQJIT.cpp's `#if CPU(X86_64)` inside EMIT_BINARY(...)):
//    macroargdirectives. A constexpr integer local initialized by a
//    class's constexpr conversion is a constant (WasmBBQJIT64.h's
//    `constexpr bool isSigned = std::is_signed<IntType>();` that `if
//    constexpr` reads): constexprconversionlocal. An rvalue for a
//    template's parameter by value and a function's `const T &` is
//    converted alike: the function wins (`makeString(const IndexOrName
//    &)` over WTF's `makeString(StringTypes...)`): rvaluevalueorconstref.
//    A function declared `extern "C"` beside C++ overloads of its name
//    keeps C's linkage at its definition (WebAssemblySuspending.cpp's
//    runWebAssemblySuspendingFunction, which IPInt calls): externcoverload.
//    What follows a return, break, continue or goto up to a label, and
//    the branch an integer constant condition does not take, are not
//    generated, as Clang does not (B3LowerMacros.cpp calls
//    Math::i64_div_u, defined for 32-bit ARM, after `if constexpr
//    (!isARM_THUMB2()) break;`): unreachableafterjump. A qualified call
//    weighs the named namespace's functions only, and an unnamed
//    namespace's directives are in force in its parent only, not
//    anywhere (simdutf's scalar::utf8::utf16_length_from_utf8 called
//    simdutf's own function of the name, which called it again):
//    qualifiedcallnodirective. A lambda in a lambda holds the class's
//    `this`, not the outer closure's address (WasmOMGIRGenerator's
//    patchpoint generators ran after their outer lambdas were gone):
//    nestedlambdathis. A cast of an object to a reference to another
//    (not a class) type is the object's own bytes, written through:
//    reinterpret_cast, and `(T &)x` with a T & not const (MachineContext
//    set a signal's instruction pointer in a temporary, and WebAssembly's
//    fault handler returned to the faulting load for ever):
//    castreferencereinterpret. A generic lambda's parameters hide the
//    function's locals of their names from `[=]` (B3's CheckSpecial
//    copied the function's CCallHelpers into its late path and freed its
//    buffer twice): genericlambdaparamshadow. A const integer local's
//    initializer read to see whether it is constant leaves no
//    temporaries behind (the FTL's OSR exit compiler destroyed a
//    RefPtr<JITCode> never made): consttemporarylocal. mlxlibcpp's
//    ranges projections reach a pointer element's member through the
//    pointer, and `p.*pm` of a pointer is an error, not the pointer's
//    own bytes (Air's stack slots sorted by `&StackSlot::offsetFromFP`
//    came out unsorted; spills overlapped the callee saves):
//    rangesprojectionpointer.
// 43: function bodies are made through mlx4's LIR, its optimizer and its
//    x86-64 back end by default (ir.mlx, irgen.mlx; `-fbackend=stack` or
//    MLX_CC_BACKEND=stack is the stack machine alone): every object's
//    code differs, the frames are sized by the values live at once, and
//    what the lowering does not cover (long double, wide integers,
//    variadic definitions, computed goto, alloca, 16-byte atomics) is
//    the stack machine's in the same object.
pub const CODEGEN_EPOCH: u64 = 53
